      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the advice. i tried some pedialyte but he just threw it right back up again. he's still super lethargic and acting kinda out of it. i really dont want to pay the hospital bill if i can avoid it... i saw online that some people use salt tablets or even a bit of table salt in water to help with electrolytes fast. would it be okay if i just mixed a little salt into his water to see if that helps lock in the hydration? how much should i give him?",
